  {
   "k": "z1inq2",
   "en": "⟦0⟧ Communism and Fascism set no positive requirement and additionally carry a hidden ⟦1⟧ modifier, so they can effectively join factions freely. ⟦2⟧ Capped at 50% during a defensive war — see below.",
   "frags": 3
  },
  {
   "k": "1i4tfqo",
   "en": "join_faction_tension = -0.1"
  },
  {
   "k": "156ew7e",
   "en": "National focuses, decisions, ideas and advisors can lower this threshold through further ⟦0⟧ modifiers.",
   "frags": 1
  },
  {
   "k": "nv4gnp",
   "en": "Defensive-war cap"
  },
  {
   "k": "985a41",
   "en": "While a country is in a ⟦0⟧, the limit used to join a faction becomes the lower of its own threshold or 50%.⟦1⟧ For example, a Democratic country that normally needs 80% World Tension can join a faction at 50% Tension while defending. (This is the cap referenced for Democratic \"Join faction\" in the table above.)",
   "frags": 2
  },
  {
   "k": "cth930",
   "en": "defensive war"
  },
  {
   "k": "oly0a4",
   "en": "Lowering the requirement with operatives"
  },
  {
   "k": "ubq8vf",
   "en": "⟦0⟧ A ⟦1⟧ operative mission can reduce the World Tension a target country needs in order to join a faction. The requirement drops by 0.001 per day per operative, up to a maximum reduction of 20% World Tension, and decays back when no operative is assigned. Multiple operatives working the same faction suffer diminishing returns (a stacking factor of 0.5 applied by efficiency rank).⟦2⟧",
   "frags": 3
  },
